{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh7PxBfUD6gPdh2fXfga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For [Ni(NH₃)₆]²⁺, **Dq = 1060 cm⁻¹** and **B ≈ 887 cm⁻¹**. Dq is set exactly by the first band. B comes from a best-fit sum rule, because no single B reproduces both upper bands exactly. C = 4.5B ≈ 3990 cm⁻¹, but that number simply follows from the assumed ratio, not from the spectrum.\n\n**Model (d⁸, octahedral, spin-allowed triplets).** The ground term is ³A₂g, at −12Dq.\n\n- The ³T₂g term lies at −2Dq, so the first band is ν₁ = 10Dq.\n- The two ³T₁g terms, ³T₁g(F) and ³T₁g(P), mix through a 2×2 matrix. Measured from the ground state, the matrix is:\n\n| | ³T₁g(F) | ³T₁g(P) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ³T₁g(F) | 18Dq | 4Dq |\n| ³T₁g(P) | 4Dq | 12Dq + 15B |\n\nOnly triplet terms appear, so C drops out of all three band energies. The C/B = 4.5 assumption therefore does not affect the fit.\n\n**Dq.** From ν₁ = 10Dq = 10 600 cm⁻¹, Dq = 1060 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The sum of the two roots equals the trace of the matrix:\n\nν₂ + ν₃ = 30Dq + 15B\n17 500 + 27 600 = 45 100 = 31 800 + 15B\nB = 887 cm⁻¹\n\n**Check.** Putting Dq = 1060 and B = 887 back into the matrix gives:\n- ν₂ ≈ 17 070 cm⁻¹ (observed 17 500)\n- ν₃ ≈ 28 030 cm⁻¹ (observed 27 600)\n\nEach band is off by about 430 cm⁻¹, which is acceptable. However, fitting B to each band separately gives different values:\n- From ν₂ alone: B ≈ 1080 cm⁻¹\n- From ν₃ alone: B ≈ 850 cm⁻¹\n\nSo the spectrum is only approximately consistent with a single B. The 887 cm⁻¹ value is the sum-rule compromise, and it is roughly 82% of the free-ion value of about 1080 cm⁻¹ for Ni²⁺.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1060, \"B\": 887, \"C\": 3990, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from nu1=10Dq; B from the T1 sum rule nu2+nu3=30Dq+15B; C=4.5B is assumed, not measured.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":857,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":857,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77d728b1-9651-435c-9b8d-576baeb829aa","uuid":"de181517-d400-4bc1-b3d9-80d33504d848","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:37:54.419Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh7PwrpJpfheR6E8JMVN"}
